 m/b/form/01a184d7582176d685d7207b4cda357b\n\nAlthough the Middle East/SWAN
 A region encompasses a diverse range of authoritarian regimes\, protests a
 re surprisingly common across much of it. Mass mobilizations such as the A
 rab uprisings and Iran’s Woman\, Life\, Freedom movement attract interna
 tional attention\, yet less is known about the thousands of smaller protes
 ts that precede and follow them. This talk will examine patterns of protes
 t across the region and explore how repression is changing in the age of m
 ass surveillance and artificial intelligence.\n\nThis event is co-sponsore
 d by CDDRL's Program on Arab Reform and Development and the Middle Eastern
  Studies Forum.\n\nABOUT THE SPEAKER\n\nJillian Schwedler is Distinguished
  Professor of Political Science at the City University of New York’s Hun
 ter College and the Graduate Center and Nonresident Senior Fellow at the C
 rown Center for the Middle East at Brandeis University. She has served in 
 elected leadership positions for the American Political Science Associatio
 n and the Middle East Studies Association. She has been a member of the Ed
 itorial Committee of the International Journal of Middle East Studies and 
 is currently Chair of the Editorial Committee for the Middle East Research
  and Information Project (MERIP)\, publishers of Middle East Report.\n\nPr
